<DocsLayout
  title="Phase 2 — Context seeding"
  description="Where Think OS becomes actually useful. The agent drafts your core context files from your connected tools."
  current="phase-2"
>
  <p>
    Phase 2 is <strong>Step 3</strong> of the three-step setup flow (install,
    restart + authenticate, then this). After install and a restart, run
    <code>/thinkos-continue</code> in a fresh Claude Code session. The agent
    walks through, in order:
  </p>

  <ol>
    <li><strong>Welcome &amp; auth check</strong> — verifies any plugin connectors needing OAuth are authorized.</li>
    <li><strong>Import an existing vault</strong> (optional) — if you have a markdown vault from Obsidian or an older Think OS install, point at it. The agent maps filenames to Think OS slots and copies content over, marking those files as seeded.</li>
    <li><strong>File picker</strong> — choose which un-seeded files to populate next.</li>
    <li><strong>Per-file flow</strong> — chip-pick which connectors to read from, see the draft, approve / edit / regenerate. Nothing writes to the vault without your OK.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Three-layer capture offer</strong> — at the end, three grouped questions set up forward-capture:
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Block 1 — Session capture</strong> (local, no API cost): a launchd job appends a one-line stub of what you worked on to your private vault every 2h during work hours.</li>
        <li><strong>Block 2 — Vault maintenance</strong> (scheduled cloud triggers): daily reindex, weekly review draft, quarterly archive, optional morning brief. Defaults are on for the first three.</li>
        <li><strong>Block 3 — Continuous capture sources</strong> (opt-in per source): Calendar snapshot (default on), Granola meetings, Linear tickets, ClickUp tickets, Gmail starred, Slack DMs + @-mentions.</li>
      </ul>
      After each block, the agent shows what was set up before moving to the next. Anything skipped here is available later via <code>/thinkos-autosave on</code>, <code>/thinkos-automate</code>, and <code>/thinkos-capture-setup</code>.
    </li>
  </ol>

  <h2>Files seeded</h2>
  <ul>
    <li><code>05 Profile/Identity.md</code> — role, working style, comm preferences.</li>
    <li><code>02 Projects/Project Index.md</code> — your active and dormant projects.</li>
    <li><code>01 Now/Current Focus.md</code> — what this week is actually about.</li>
    <li><code>03 People/People.md</code> — frequent collaborators with context.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Full playbook</h2>
  <p>
    For the agent-facing playbook this flow follows, see
    <a href="https://github.com/dhirajsapkal/think-os/blob/main/docs/phase-2-seeding-playbook.md">
      docs/phase-2-seeding-playbook.md
    </a>.
  </p>
</DocsLayout>
